Company Background
 Our client is a global technology company transforming the way brands and agencies make marketing decisions. Its platform enables marketers to plan and activate cross-channel, programmatic media campaigns using real-time research, proprietary audience data, advanced analytics, and more than 150 integrated partners including Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, Snapchat, and Twitter. The company operates across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia, and Australia.
 Project Description
 The role is focused on developing and modernizing real-time DSP serving services that process bid requests, deliver ads, integrate with third-party platforms, and record measurement events used for reporting and billing. The team works on high-throughput, low-latency systems processing millions of requests per second, with a strong focus on availability, data correctness, performance tuning, and scaling the platform for future growth. Current initiatives include splitting a monolith into microservices, improving deployment automation, and moving measurement pipelines from batch processing to real-time streaming with Kafka.
 Technologies
 Java
 Kafka / Kinesis
 Redis
 S3
 Tomcat
 Docker, K8S
 Git, CI/CD
 What You'll Do
 Develop critical high-performance, large-scale services for DSP programmatic integrations and platform products;
 Work closely with the Product team to understand business needs and translate product requirements into technical solutions;
 Write clean, efficient, and production-ready code with a strong focus on high throughput and low latency;
 Design, develop, test, and improve new and existing platform features;
 Contribute to building large-scale distributed systems processing billions of transactions per day under strict SLAs;
 Improve test coverage, monitoring coverage, automation, and overall system observability;
 Follow Agile methodologies and work in a fast-paced engineering environment with quick delivery cycles;
 Job Requirements
 5+ years of commercial experience in Java backend development, with a focus on scalable backend systems;
 Strong knowledge of the JVM ecosystem, including garbage collection, profiling, and performance tuning;
 Experience with distributed REST APIs, fault tolerance, scalability, consistency, and resilience;
 Hands-on experience with low-latency and high-throughput services;
 Experience with real-time streaming pipelines using Kafka, Kinesis, or similar technologies;
 Strong knowledge of data structures and algorithms;
 Experience with web/application servers such as Tomcat;
 Solid understanding of networking and load balancing concepts;
 Production experience with Docker and Kubernetes;
 Experience with Git and CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab CI/CD or similar tools;
 Interest in applying modern technologies and AI-assisted development tools;
 Readiness to participate in PagerDuty rotation (1 week per quarter);
 Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to explain complex technical trade-offs to both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
 English: B2 or higher;
 Nice To Have
 Prior experience in the AdTech industry;
 Familiarity with Python or Scala;
 What Do We Offer
 The global benefits package includes:
 Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;
 Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;
 Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;
 Health insurance;
 Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;
 Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;
 Referral program for bringing in new talent;
 Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.

Do you pride yourself on being the person who can actually find anything online? Then the Surfshark SEO team wants you.

We optimize Surfshark's website to bring in a steady flow of organic traffic across multiple search engines. Join us and you'll work at the intersection of tech, content, and localization — alongside on-site, off-page, and technical SEO specialists, content producers, copywriters, and web content specialists. If you're curious, inventive, and want a team that actually rewards those instincts, keep reading.




IF YOU WANT TO:

 - Drive organic growth through on-site SEO, with a focus on localized markets;

 - Spot and act on new SEO opportunities from competitor analysis, search trends, and keyword research;

 - Improve existing content with a data-driven, user-first approach;

 - Run content production, coordinating with writers, localization managers, and WP designers;

 - Monitor, analyze, and report on how our SEO is performing;

 - Experiment with AI Search optimization and make it work for us;

 - Sharpen workflows through automation;

 - Watch global SEO trends and find smart ways to put them to use.




AND YOU CAN CHECK OFF:

 - Proven experience of driving organic growth through smart SEO strategy;

 - A solid grasp of SEO best practices;

 - Confidence with SEO and analytics tools like Ahrefs and Google Search Console;

 - An eye for content that's both easy to read and built to rank;

 - An analytical, data-driven way of making decisions;

 - A habit of tracking AI Search developments and testing what actually works;

 - Clear communication and a collaborative streak;

 - Familiarity with international SEO and multilingual websites.




HERE’S THE DEAL:

 - Growth and learning opportunities: time dedicated to learning, conferences, online learning platforms, and books for your professional development;

 - Health and wellness: we want you to feel and be your best. That's why we offer various benefits, from online workouts, a physical coach and a gym to regular mental health checks;

 - Tools of your choice: choose technical equipment and the tools you need to do your best;

 - Community and celebrations: get ready for long-lasting traditions such as yearly workation, Friday get-togethers, various team buildings and company celebrations;

 - Convenient commuting: traveling from point A to point B can be a pain. That’s why, depending on your unique circumstances, we compensate part of your public transport costs;

 - Work-life balance: We encourage working in the office, with the possibility of up to two remote days per week. Plus, with our WFA policy, you can work from almost anywhere in the world;

 - Premium Surfshark accounts: for you, your family, and friends;

 - Gross salary: 2700-4150 Eur/month for the Lithuanian market, 10600-19400 Pln/month for the Polish market. It may vary depending on your skills and experience.

